OL,3,GNEWSA'Parking costs mean our customers
OL,4,Aare going elsewhere'
OL,5,
OL,6,FFewer residents are shopping in York
OL,7,Fsince the city council's 2025 decision
OL,8,Fto increase parking charges, a business
OL,9,Fleader has said.
OL,11,FAndrew Lowson, director of York
OL,12,FBusiness Improvement District, was
OL,13,Fspeaking as the council voted to cut
OL,14,Fprices in some community car parks for
OL,15,Fvehicles displaying a valid permit or
OL,16,FMinster Badge.
OL,18,F"Businesses have consistently told us
OL,19,Fthat visits are becoming shorter and
OL,20,Fthat regular customers cite parking
OL,21,Fcosts for going elsewhere," Lowson
OL,22,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,388,380,200,160,0,100
